ggml-webgpu: batched mat-vec and tiled-matmul knobs for prompt MUL_MAT on Adreno (round 5).

POCO F5 Pro (Adreno 740), PLaMo 3 0.8B, round-4 per-op run of a 38-token prompt: the tiled
q4_K / q6_K matmul (n > 4) took 78% of the prompt graph. Without subgroup matrices the tiled
shader computes 32x32 outputs per 64-thread workgroup (4x4 per thread), dequantizes each 32-wide
K tile of the weights into f16 shared memory once per 32-column N tile, and reads 8 scalar f16
values from shared memory per 16 FMAs with tile rows 256 bytes apart (all 8 threads of a tile row
on one bank). For n = 38 it also computes 64 columns.

- Batched mat-vec: for 4 < n <= bmv (Adreno default 64; token bmv0 = off, bmv8..256), MUL_MAT with
  2D operands goes through the workgroup-reduction mat-vec shader in batches of 4 columns
  (bmvc2/bmvc8), one dispatch for the full batches (as broadcast2 batches) and one for the rest.
  The columns of a batch share one read and dequantization of the weights.
- Tiled matmul knobs (off by default): mmt4x4|8x4|4x8|8x8 outputs per thread, mmwg8x8|16x8|8x16|
  16x16|8x4|16x4 threads, mmpad (shared-memory rows padded to TILE_K + 2 halves; float types and
  k-quants only). Shapes over 16 KiB of workgroup storage or 256 invocations fall back to 4x4 x 8x8.
- Adreno SOFT_MAX / fused RMS_NORM row workgroups 128 (round-4 sweep: rwg128 best); rwg256 restores.
- Native only: SAKUTTO_WEBGPU_TRACE_PIPELINES=1 lists the shader variants a run compiles.

